WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.801
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.834
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.534
You're here.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.601
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.868
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:11.200
Guys, it seems like there's
so much going on right now.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.234
Father's Day is this Sunday.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.901
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.767
Congress just held another
hearing about January 6th.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.734
The first photo
of Ryan Gosling as Ken...

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.467
...in the "Barbie" movie is out.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.200
And I just heard Jack Daniels
is teaming up with Coca-Cola

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.167
to sell a canned Jack &amp; Coke.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.400
There's a lot to go over,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.200
so let's just jump in
and cover it all at once.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.067
It's time for a "News Smash."
Here we go.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.567
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.300
♪♪

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.767
First up, this Sunday
is Father's Day.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.434
It is the time to thank your dad

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:51.968
for everything
he's done for you.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.234
It's a fun day to celebrate,
but you know what's not so fun?

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.868
The congressional hearings.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.534
[ Laughter ]
They're investigating
January 6th.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.901
That's when a mob went
after Mike Pence,

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.701
who, by the way, has as much
going on below the belt as

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.467
A Ken doll.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.234
What can you do, you know?

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.434
He's a Ken doll.
I mean,

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.934
and Ken and Barbie,
they're a great couple.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.534
I mean, they go together like

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.767
Jack &amp; Coke.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.968
Now, you can get it
as a premixed cocktail,

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.534
which is good news
if you still need a gift for

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:21.534
Father's Day.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:22.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.467
Your dad deserves
something special.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.868
Because it's not easy
raising kids.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.267
I mean, before he had you,
your dad probably looked like

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
Ryan Gosling. I mean,

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.167
just look at him.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.901
If that Ken walked
into a bachelorette party,

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:34.901
there'd be a full-on

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.534
Riot.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:37.968
People stormed the Capitol,

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.868
and took selfies
while they did it.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.834
You know, they must've pregamed
with a few

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.634
canned cocktails.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:45.300
If you drink one, you drink six.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.868
I mean, they go down
real smooth.

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:47.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.667
Speaking of down and smooth...

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:50.901
Poor Ken.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.501
He'll never be able to be a

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.534
Dad. So...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.767
...in conclusion --

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.267
Nice abs.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.634
Tastes bad.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.167
Make it stop.

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:04.901
[ Laughter ]
Love you, Pop.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
This has been a "News Smash."

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.100
♪♪

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.834
Thank you very much.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.634
As I mentioned,
this Sunday is Father's Day.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.267
-Four?
-Four people, yeah.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.901
[ Laughter ]
That's great.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.200
Yeah, it's the day we thank Dad
for all the times

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.734
we went to him with a problem
and he said --

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:24.434
[ Changes accent ]
"Ask your mother."

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.067
On Father's Day,
you don't even have

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.868
to make breakfast in bed
because there's always

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.000
a half a baloney sandwich
on his nightstand.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.334
Let's be honest --
no one cares about Father's Day.

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.300
[ Laughter ]
Even the Hallmark Channel

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.868
does nothing for Father's Day.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.167
[ Awws and laughter ]
Seriously, they'll air

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.434
an Arbor Day marathon
before a Father's Day movie.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:43.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:44.834
Yeah, Father's Day is
a lot different

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.501
than Mother's Day.
On Mother's Day,

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.334
every card looks like a novel.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.534
On Father's Day, you basically
get the CliffsNotes.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:54.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:55.734
Meanwhile, leading up
to Father's Day,

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:58.501
Kingsford released a new ad
for their charcoal.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:01.267
It might just be me,
but it seems a little strange.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:02.000
Watch this --

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.200
-This...

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.534
...gather around the grill
with...

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:08.501
because a Kingsford flame is the
perfect thing to stare at to...

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:11.968
[ Laughter ]
Squirt the lighter fluid.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.934
Listen to him say...

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.067
...and realize it's
as close to...

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.601
as he's ever going to get.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.701
[ Laughter ]
Stand there as he retells
the story of how...

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.334
[ Laughter ]
Finally work up
the courage to...

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:27.968
[ Laughter ]
Then listen to him reply...

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.534
[ Laughter and whistling ]

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
-That's right. Beautiful.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.734
Well, this is fun --
the Westminster Dog Show

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.434
kicks off tomorrow
right here in New York.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:50.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.033
Breeds are categorized
into groups,

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:55.200
including working,
sporting, and non-sporting.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.634
It's the same way
dads classify their sons.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.400
[ Changes accent ]
I got one working,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.734
one non-sporting.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.300
One not working.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.400
Get this --
I read that President Biden

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.801
will soon release his plan
for the next pandemic.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.133
Americans were like, "Awesome.

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.434
Wait, what next pandemic?"

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.601
It's not much.
All they're planning to do is

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:18.501
mail everyone
a sour dough starter kit.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:21.734
No, I'm kidding.
It's a highly detailed plan

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.534
called "Tiger King" Season 3.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:24.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.567
Well, guys, gas prices
are still soaring

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:29.000
and experts say that there's
no relief in sight.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.868
With that in mind, we went
to our sound engineer,

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.400
Steve Mandel,
who's going to tell us

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.200
what he thinks about gas prices,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.334
in a new segment called
"Steve Mandel's Rant Zone."

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.868
[ Laughter ]
-This is...

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:40.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
...the only place where you're

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:44.000
going to get...

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.100
If you can't handle the heat,

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.601
[ Laughter ]
stay away from the flames

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:48.300
because Steve Mandel...

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.701
...and...

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:51.434
And now, it's time to find out
what goes on

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:52.467
in the mind of this man.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.000
-[ Sedately ]
I think gas prices are
too high.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:01.400
-This has been...

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.534
Consider yourself ranted.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.634
-[ Sedately ]
Don't forget to smash
that like button.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:11.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.334
-Some entertainment news --

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:17.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.701
I heard that a new Marvel
series, called "Wonder Man,"

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.901
is in the works at Disney+.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:24.934
Finally, a superhero
for boys to relate to.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:30.200
Yep, Wonder Man has superhuman
strength, speed, stamina,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.467
and the ability to fight
copyright infringement lawsuits

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:33.300
from "Superman."

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.534
Actually, Wonder Man's
super power is

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.033
hearing what Wonder Woman said
in the meeting

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.234
and then repeating it louder.

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:40.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:41.434
[ Booing ]

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.601
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.534
Hey, guys, I saw that
this Saturday is

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:50.534
Paul McCartney's 80th birthday.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:54.567
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:58.067
And I want to be real
for a moment.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.601
His music means so much to me,
so, to honor him,

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:04.033
here's a special performance
of his most beautiful song,

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:04.901
"Let It Be."

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:09.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:21.601
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:22.801
[ Nervous laugh ]

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:24.567
Whew!

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.968
[ Nervous laugh ]
I know the rights to this

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.367
are super expensive, but, uh --

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:31.634
I hope we cleared them.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:35.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:38.367
[ Stage muted ]
-♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:40.901
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:44.033
♪ And on his farm,
he had some pigs ♪

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:46.567
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:49.567
♪ With an oink-oink here
and an oink-oink there ♪

00:06:49.567 --> 00:06:52.567
♪ Here an oink, there an oink,
everywhere an oink-oink ♪

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:55.300
♪ Old MacDonald had a farm ♪

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.300
♪ E-I-E-I-O ♪

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.367
-Thank you very much.

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:01.567
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:04.133
Thank you for the music,
Sir Paul.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:06.400
[ Whistling ]

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.067
Hey, guys, I saw that LEGO's
is spending more than $1 billion

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:13.033
to build its first factory
in the U.S.

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.567
-Whoo!
-Yep, it will probably
take a while to build

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.834
because, halfway through,
they realize,

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.501
one brick's missing
and have to start over.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:22.167
Well, you guys,
summer is officially here

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.968
and I read that today
is National Flip-Flop Day.

00:07:24.968 --> 00:07:25.767
That's pretty fun.

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:27.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:29.834
-No, wait, wait.
-I love flip flops.

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:32.801
-Like, okay,
you love flip-flops.

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.901
What else?
-I mean, I mean, I like --

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:37.467
I like flip-flops.
I like tank tops.

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.968
-That's cool.
What else?

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:40.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:43.501
-I like pawn shops
and bus stops.

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.968
I like listening to hip hop,
K-Pop, and doo-wop

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:48.567
nonstop at a coffee shop
on my laptop.

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:51.367
I like eating lamb chops
with Carrot Top and Fetty Wap,

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:52.968
drinking peach schnapps,
watching "RoboCop"

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:54.901
at a rooftop of a co-op.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:57.133
[ Laughter ]
♪ I like rock steady, not bebop,
brooms, not mops ♪

00:07:57.133 --> 00:07:59.300
♪ Sucking gumdrops
and lollipops with bellhops ♪

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.701
♪ Jamming is easy,
topping the sounds ♪

00:08:00.701 --> 00:08:02.267
♪ Of Alka-Seltzer going
plop, plop ♪

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:03.400
-♪ Fizz, fizz ♪

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.801
♪ Oh, what a relief it ♪

00:08:04.801 --> 00:08:07.400
-♪ Is...it nice to be naughty? ♪

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.033
♪ Is it naughty to be nice? ♪

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.467
-♪ Okay, okay, okay ♪
-♪ Is it naughty to be nice? ♪

00:08:11.467 --> 00:08:12.534
♪ Naughty to be ♪
-♪ Okay ♪

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:13.400
-♪ Okay ♪

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:17.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.667
[ Whistling ]

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:22.601
Listen to this -- a motorcyclist
in Minnesota was arrested

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:25.300
for going 144 miles per hour

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.901
and he said
that he was going that fast

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:28.667
to cool off from the heat.

00:08:28.667 --> 00:08:31.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:32.467
It actually worked
because he got to ride

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:33.901
in an air-conditioned
police car.

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:35.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.434 --> 00:08:37.734
And, finally, like I said,
this Sunday is Father's Day

00:08:37.734 --> 00:08:39.367
and there are so many
amazing dads out there

00:08:39.367 --> 00:08:40.701
who do such great things

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:42.634
and the one thing we all know
dads can do

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:43.901
is dance.

00:08:43.901 --> 00:08:45.767
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:08:45.767 --> 00:08:48.467
So, we went down to the streets
and asked dads to show us

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:51.000
their best moves
to celebrate Father's Day.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.934
Here's some great dad dancing.

00:08:52.934 --> 00:08:56.434
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:58.801
-♪ My money don't
jiggle, jiggle, it folds ♪

00:08:58.801 --> 00:09:01.300
♪ I'd like to see you
wiggle, wiggle, for sure ♪

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.701
♪ It makes me wanna
dribble, dribble, you know ♪

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:06.100
♪ Riding in my Fiat,
you really have to see it ♪

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.100
♪ Six feet two in a compact,
no slack ♪

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.200
♪ Luckily the seats go back,
I've got a knack ♪

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.434
♪ To relax in my mind,
sipping some ♪

00:09:13.434 --> 00:09:15.801
[ Electronic voice ]
♪ Red, red wine ♪

00:09:15.801 --> 00:09:16.901
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:18.634
-Happy Father's Day!

